  "body": "Refs #1448. Part of #1448.\n\nDepends on #3324 (the shared mechanism). Do not start before #3324 is merged. The `blocked` label goes when #3324 is closed.\n\n## What happens\n\nSinker Burn has a burn position `x`, `y` (`crates/app/src/operation/types/sinker.rs:29-30`) and an orbit (`:57`). Sinker Side Burn has `burn`, `direction`, `amount` and `undersize` (`sinker.rs:151-160`). The burn position is where the electrode works. It is not a start pick. The user cannot set where the orbit or the side move starts, or where it ends.\n\n## Expected\n\n- Sinker Burn: the start pick sets the start angle of the orbit around the burn position. The exit pick sets where the orbit ends before the retract.\n- Sinker Side Burn: the start pick chooses the side where the side move begins. The exit pick chooses where it ends.\n- If a kind has no free start for a given orbit (for example no orbit), its row says so by name.\n\nSeams: the arms `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs:87` (SinkerBurn, with `compensation_refusal`) and `:95` (SinkerSideBurn, with `refusal`).\n\n## Laws a pick must keep (refused by name, never moved)\n\n- The compensation refusal and the side burn refusal keep their laws.\n- The orbit at the start angle stays inside the cavity limits (`cavity_x`, `cavity_y`).\n- The wear and the undersize laws hold.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A pin test for each kind shows the start at the pick and the end at the exit pick.\n- A pin test shows an impossible pick refused by name.\n- Undo and redo restore the previous path. MCP `edit_operation` sets the picks.\n- Every shipped sinker golden without a pick is byte-identical.\n\nSafety floor: this changes toolpaths and posted G-code.\n",
